A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus tells of a man who seeks fruit on a fig tree three years and finds none, orders it cut down, and hears a request for one year more, with two outcomes stated and neither given. Jesus gives no explanation and names none of the parts. Jesus also likens this generation to children in the market whose calls go unanswered, and says that John and the Son of man were each met with a charge. The fig tree says that fruit is looked for, that time is given and that the end is stated. The comparison says that a refusal finds a charge against any coming.'))
